    interpreter_wrong_owner_arg_overload_fallthrough_2026_11_27, fixing, p3sweep4-20261127, 2026-11-27T19:35:05Z, 2026-11-27T19:35:05Z, open, "wave9"

    interpreter_wrong_owner_arg_overload_fallthrough_2026_11_27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4-61127: reproduced (driver imports qc.Thing but calls qb's overloaded show(i64)/show(Thing) with a wrong-owner instance: before wrongowner=11 exit 0 - silently ran the class-typed overload; SIMPLE_DEBUG_DUPDISPATCH showed all scoring rejected then a P5-flat flat-map entry; the JIT lane raises the correct AmbiguousCallable (owner decision 2026-11-09) but demotes to the interpreter which then succeeded with the wrong answer - the interpreter was the last line of defense). Root cause: evaluate_identifier_user_call Priority 4 (interpreter_call/mod.rs ~1068-1075): when select_overload rejects every candidate, selection silently degraded to the arity-only candidate_declared_by fallback then Priority 5's flat-map functions.get(name) (last-registration-wins, no type check); the scoring itself was correct (owner-exact identity rejects the foreign Thing). Fix (92 insertions, no deletions, interpreter_call/mod.rs not TAKEN): new provable_class_rejection() returns the demangled class name only when some argument carries a concrete class identity (aggregate_class) that every arity-compatible candidate's typed parameter rejects (same owner-scoped comparison as overload_score) - erased/untyped values never trigger it; when provable, the arity-only fallback is suppressed and the call returns CompileError E1003 ambiguous call to show: argument of class Thing selects none of the overloads. Spec test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/wrong_owner_arg_overload_spec.spl (3 its: right-owner control, interpreter lane errors, JIT lane errors after demotion) RED 1/3 on fresh seed, GREEN 3/3 on scratch; controls main_flat/main_alias_neg/main_entry_neg unchanged; same_name_class specs 7/7, 5/5, 1/1 identical to baseline; static_method_overload_dispatch 4/4, export_use_alias_owner 2/2. Residuals: the SINGLE-overload case still falls through Priority 5 (same wrong-code shape, outside the doc scope - follow-up); the pure-Simple AST interpreter has broader warn-only last-write-wins dispatch debt for co-compiled names (different documented debt, separate item recommended); candidate count omitted from the error deliberately (registered set holds $dupN twins). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/wrong_owner_arg_overload_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_owner_identity_spec.spl"
    interpreter_wrong_owner_arg_overload_fallthrough_2026_11_27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: reproduced (wrong-owner instance silently ran the class-typed overload: wrongowner=11 exit 0; all scoring rejected then a P5-flat flat-map entry; the JIT AmbiguousCallable demoted to the interpreter which succeeded with the wrong answer). Root cause: evaluate_identifier_user_call Priority 4 silently degraded to the arity-only candidate_declared_by fallback then Priority 5 flat-map functions.get (last-registration-wins). Fix (interpreter_call/mod.rs +92): provable_class_rejection() returns the demangled class name only when an argument carries concrete class identity that every arity-compatible candidate's typed parameter rejects (erased/untyped never trigger); when provable the arity fallback is suppressed and the call returns E1003 ambiguous call. Spec wrong_owner_arg_overload RED 1/3 to GREEN 3/3 on the scratch build; controls unchanged; same_name_class specs 7/7, 5/5, 1/1; static_method_overload_dispatch 4/4, export_use_alias_owner 2/2. General native-build path verified clean after the change (hello-world native-build produced, zero ambiguous-call errors). Residuals: single-overload Priority-5 fallthrough remains (outside the doc scope); pure-Simple AST interpreter warn-only last-write-wins dispatch debt is a separate documented item. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/wrong_owner_arg_overload_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_owner_identity_spec.spl"
